# Playback and downloads

`src/playback/` owns the player. Export a `PlayerEngine` (load album, play, pause, next, previous, seekBy ±10, skipTo, setRate, subscribe to status). V1 adapter: `react-native-nitro-player` `1.7.0-alpha.2` `TrackPlayer` + `PlayerQueue` with `repeat: 'off'`. Do not import `react-native-nitro-player` outside this folder. Do not add a second adapter in V1. Do not use nitro-player `DownloadManager`, Cast, or equalizer (Phase 5 stays `@kesha-antonov/react-native-background-downloader` + `react-native-notify-kit`).

Queue is a **single album**; playback **stops at the last track**. `loadAlbum` copies a **frozen session** (`albumId` + track `id`/`url`s) into one native playlist. Catalogue refresh updates Home/Library only — it must not rebuild the live queue. If the playing album or track is omitted from a new catalogue, keep playing the session until it ends. Native playlists are not the catalogue source of truth; prune extras on album load.

Resume **per album id** only:

```ts
{ [albumId]: { trackId: string; positionSec: number; updatedAt: number } }
```

Playback rate is **per album**, `0.25`–`2.0` in `0.25` steps, default `1.0`. Persist separately from resume position. `loadAlbum` applies that album’s saved rate. Now Playing rate control is Phase 3. iOS lock-screen rate buttons are `0.5, 1.0, 1.25, 1.5, 1.75, 2.0` (no `0.25` / `0.75`). Android has no rate media button.

Configure once: `showInNotification: true`, `carPlayEnabled` / `androidAutoEnabled` false, `remoteSkipForwardInterval` / `remoteSkipBackwardInterval` `10`. `PlayerConfig` has no extra flags — JS packs `icon:notification_icon`, `skipOnError`, and `remotePrimary` into `androidNotificationIcon`. Native `applyConfigToken` sets Android `notificationSmallIconResName` from `icon:` (drawable `notification_icon`, copied at prebuild by `plugins/with-android-notification-icon.js`). Lock screen / notification / Bluetooth Now Playing come from the native media session. In-app always shows both prev/next and ±10.

**Remote primary** (Settings, default ±10 / `"seek"`): compact notification, lock screen, Bluetooth, and car follow this pair. The other pair is **secondary** — in-app plus Android expanded notification overflow. `setRemotePrimary("seek" | "skip")` reconfigures native. Headset prev/next (`SEEK_TO_PREVIOUS` / `NEXT`, iOS `previousTrack`/`nextTrack`) follow primary. When primary is ±10, Android overflow prev/next are custom session commands so hardware can seek without also remapping expanded skip. Media3 disables `SEEK_TO_NEXT` on the last item — the `ForwardingPlayer` **adds** that command (and seek-forward) when primary is seek so Bluetooth +10 still works mid last-track. Do not strip commands or wrap session listeners (that dropped the notification). iOS cannot split next/prev: remapping them for Bluetooth also remaps Control Center next/prev; track skip stays in-app when primary is ±10. Needs a new native build after install (`npx expo run:ios` / `android`); iOS `UIBackgroundModes: audio`.

Lock screen / notification Previous still uses the library default when primary is track skip (~2s into the track restarts it; earlier than that goes to the previous track; first track restarts at 0). Android System UI would otherwise call ExoPlayer `seekToPrevious` on a windowed timeline — the patch routes `SEEK_TO_PREVIOUS` / `NEXT` through `skipToPreviousOnQueue` / `skipToNextOnQueue` when primary is skip, and through overflowing ±10 when primary is seek. ±10 overflow at track boundaries is the same patch (`seekBackOverflowing` / `seekForwardOverflowing`, iOS `seekByOnQueue`): leftover time lands on the prev/next track; first-track −10 stays at 0; last-track +10 stays at the end. Do not override `getAvailableCommands` or wrap MediaSession player listeners (that dropped the notification). Next on the last track may still show; tapping it is a no-op because skip-next uses the logical album queue. `updateTracks` also skipped the current track unless the URL was empty — the same patch allows same-URL title/artist refresh on language change. Remote skip / headset prev persist resume from **fresh native state** (track change first, then MMKV). Do not flush the previous track.

User pause rewinds `PAUSE_REWIND_SEC` (2) and persists that position so resume orients the listener. Clamp at 0; do not overflow to the previous track. Applies to in-app, lock screen, sleep timer, and Bluetooth pause. Do **not** rewind when the track or album has ended (`reason === "end"` / native `stopped`) — that looped the last track.

Now Playing calls the engine, not nitro-player APIs: prev, next, −10s, play/pause, +10s. Second row: sleep timer, add bookmark, bookmarks, read along (`https://sttm.co/{currenScripture.sttmCoSlug}/{currentTrack.startAng}`). Hide read along if the current track has no `startAng` or the current scripture has no `sttmCoSlug`. Add bookmark opens `/now-playing/bookmark-note` (optional note) before saving. Album screens open that album’s bookmarks even when nothing is playing (`/a/{albumId}/bookmarks` or `/album/{albumId}/bookmarks`). Tapping a bookmark loads that track and **plays**.

Sleep timer: end of this track, remaining tracks through end of album, after N tracks, or hours+minutes (no seconds). Pause via the engine. Note: Track/album timer options use `durationSec` on recorded tracks (`sehaj_paath`, `audiobook`). `radio` has live tracks, which have no duration — hide those options for live tracks.

Play errors: surface `PlayerStatus.error` on Now Playing and the mini player in a reserved two-line slot (layout must not jump). Tap play to retry. Do not auto-play on foreground restore after an error or after the album ends. Native skip-on-source-error is **off** by default; `setSkipOnSourceError(true)` re-enables the library’s skip-to-next. Android leaves ExoPlayer’s `playerError` and sends Media3 `SessionError` (code name only — no app copy) so the shade/lock screen can show a failed state. iOS lock screen has no error slot; pause + play-to-retry is the signal. Buffering uses `PlayerStatus.buffering`. Keep-awake stays on while playing **or** buffering. Do not add `expo-keep-awake` to `app.json` plugins (it has no config plugin; Expo would load RN `index.js` and Metro would fail).

Interruptions (calls, maps, notifications): use the library’s native audio-focus / `AVAudioSession` defaults. Pause for a call, auto-resume when the system says `shouldResume` / focus returns. Do not JS-pause on those events (that would look like a user pause and block auto-resume). Ducking (maps, some alerts) stays ducked. Headphone unplug stays paused. Do not add a keep-alive hack.

Downloads: `@kesha-antonov/react-native-background-downloader` (`skipMmkvDependency: true` with MMKV). Warn before downloading on mobile network. Batch album or per track; re-attach after process death. One `react-native-notify-kit` progress notification per batch album download; separate notifications for individual track downloads. Prefer local file if present, else stream. Index by `trackId` + URL. Do not cancel an in-flight download because a catalogue refresh omitted that track; finish it and mark **orphan** if `trackId` is absent from the live catalogue and not in the current session. Prune orphans only when they are not playing and not downloading. Offline banner when the network is gone. After reinstall an, give user option restore the cloud **wanted-offline** id list to re-download.

When a track is about to play, prefer the local file if it exists; if an in-queue offline file was deleted outside the app, skip/fail without crashing. App UI must not delete an in-queue download; the engine still has to handle files removed by the user or OS.

Car V1: lock screen / notification / Bluetooth Now Playing from the adapter. Car browse/queue is later (not V1).
